{"key":"c4cb5351207e53f3","source_file":"Potts Re.json","source_id":37371,"source_url":"concordance-repeat-ppl-repetere","term":"Repeat","headwords":["Repeat","Repetition"],"latin":["Repetere","Repetitio"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Repeat"],"latin":["Repetere"]},{"english":["Repetition"],"latin":["Repetitio"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AC","DMin","DP"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"435","subsection":"end"},"text":"(Repetition implies a different signification.) AC 707. AC 734. AC 1015.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"683","subsection":"end"},"text":"That the one word is repeated (implies the heavenly marriage).","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"734","subsection":"end"},"text":"There is no repetition (in the Word).","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"1259","subsection":"3"},"text":"Otherwise it would be an empty repetition. AC 1860:end. AC 3614.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"2033","subsection":null},"text":"The repetition of the covenant denotes a closer union.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"2034","subsection":null},"text":"The repetition of the word thou. Explained.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"2051","subsection":"2"},"text":"(This repetition shows that...)","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"3880","subsection":"end"},"text":"These appear like empty repetitions. AC 5502.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"4137","subsection":"end"},"text":"These repetitions are nowhere empty...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"4691","subsection":null},"text":"Appears to be a repetition for the sake of emphasis.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"5888","subsection":null},"text":"Where there appears to be a repetition, one expression relates to the will, and the other to the understanding. AC 6343:3. AC 7945. DSS 81. DSS 84. DSS 86.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"6378","subsection":null},"text":"Appears like a repetition of the same Thing.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"6551","subsection":"2"},"text":"Why this frequent repetition.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"8933","subsection":null},"text":"Iteration or repetition involves by all means...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"9565","subsection":null},"text":"Repeated three times = each single thing; and, in the internal sense, plenary conjunction. AC 9647.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"9661","subsection":null},"text":"The repetition involves each and all things, consequently, everywhere. AC 9923.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"DP","section":"193","subsection":null},"text":"(Reason of the repetitions in the Writings.)","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"DMin","section":"4763","subsection":null},"text":"Many repetitions (of penalties).","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"repeat-c4cb53","url":"/meta/potts/repeat-c4cb53/"}